# Hadoop 1.2.1 Single Node Installation Guide

## Step 1: Update Package Repository

```bash
sudo apt-get update
```

---

## Step 2: Configure SSH

Generate an SSH key:

```bash
ssh-keygen
```

Enable passwordless SSH login:

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

---

## Step 3: Install Java (OpenJDK 8)

```bash
sudo apt-get install openjdk-8-jdk -y
```

Verify Java installation:

```bash
java -version
```

---

## Step 4: Download Hadoop 1.2.1

Move to the home directory:

```bash
cd ~
```

Download Hadoop:

```bash
wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/hadoop/core/hadoop-1.2.1/hadoop-1.2.1.tar.gz
```

Extract the downloaded archive:

```bash
tar -xzvf hadoop-1.2.1.tar.gz
```

Move Hadoop to `/usr/local`:

```bash
sudo mv hadoop-1.2.1 /usr/local/hadoop
```

---

## Step 5: Configure Environment Variables

Open the `.bashrc` file:

```bash
vi ~/.bashrc
```

Add the following lines at the end of the file:

```bash
export HADOOP_PREFIX=/usr/local/hadoop/
export PATH=$PATH:$HADOOP_PREFIX/bin
export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-8-openjdk-amd64
export PATH=$PATH:$JAVA_HOME
```

Save and exit.

---

## Step 6: Configure Hadoop Environment

Open Hadoop environment configuration:

```bash
vi /usr/local/hadoop/conf/hadoop-env.sh
```

Add:

```bash
export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-8-openjdk-amd64
export HADOOP_OPTS=-Djava.net.preferIPV4Stack=true
```

Save and exit.

---

## Step 7: Configure core-site.xml

Open:

```bash
vi /usr/local/hadoop/conf/core-site.xml
```

Add:

```xml
<property>
    <name>fs.default.name</name>
    <value>hdfs://localhost:9000</value>
</property>

<property>
    <name>hadoop.tmp.dir</name>
    <value>/usr/local/hadoop/tmp</value>
</property>
```

Save and exit.

---

## Step 8: Configure hdfs-site.xml

Open:

```bash
vi /usr/local/hadoop/conf/hdfs-site.xml
```

Add:

```xml
<property>
    <name>dfs.replication</name>
    <value>1</value>
</property>
```

Save and exit.

---

## Step 9: Configure mapred-site.xml

Open:

```bash
vi /usr/local/hadoop/conf/mapred-site.xml
```

Add:

```xml
<property>
    <name>mapred.job.tracker</name>
    <value>hdfs://localhost:9001</value>
</property>
```

Save and exit.

---

## Step 10: Create Hadoop Temporary Directory

```bash
mkdir /usr/local/hadoop/tmp
```

---

## Step 11: Reload Environment Variables

```bash
exec bash
```

---

## Step 12: Format the Hadoop NameNode

```bash
hadoop namenode -format
```

---

## Step 13: Start Hadoop Services

```bash
start-all.sh
```

---

## Step 14: Verify Hadoop Daemons

```bash
jps
```

Expected output should contain:

* NameNode
* DataNode
* SecondaryNameNode
* JobTracker
* TaskTracker

